# Line-ending policy.
#
# TASK-DEPLOY-HOTFIX-001. The repository had no .gitattributes, and the Windows
# development checkouts run with core.autocrlf=true — so every file, including
# the Dockerfile and every shell script, landed on disk with CRLF.
#
# That is invisible on the Linux deploy server (its checkout is LF) but it makes
# the image unbuildable on Windows: `/bin/sh` reads the trailing CR as part of
# the token and a multi-line RUN script dies with
#     syntax error: unexpected word (expecting "do")   → exit code 2
# which is indistinguishable, in a build log, from a real failure of the step.
#
# Anything the container executes, or that is executed to build it, is pinned to
# LF here so it is byte-identical on every developer machine and on the server.

*               text=auto

# Shell and container tooling — must be LF wherever they are checked out.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile    text eol=lf
docker-compose*.yml  text eol=lf
.github/**/*.yml     text eol=lf
docker/**/*.conf     text eol=lf
docker/**/*.ini      text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
